  "summary": "The founding goth look: black lace, fishnet, teased backcombed hair, white makeup and post-punk gloom.",
  "description": "Around the Batcave club (Soho, 1982) and bands like Bauhaus, Siouxsie and the Banshees and The Sisters of Mercy, a coherent dress language formed: black from head to toe, fishnets, velvet, leather, backcombed black hair, pale face with dark eyes, silver jewelry of bats and ankhs. It draws on Victorian mourning dress, horror cinema and glam. The trunk of the goth family tree from which romantic, cyber and pastel branches descend.",
